# Machine-specific environment overrides for the TejaForce SDK pipeline.
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and set values for your machine.
# Variables already set in your shell always take precedence over .env
# (same semantics as python-dotenv's load_dotenv(override=False)).

# ==========================================================================
# SWITCHING HARNESS + PROVIDER
# ==========================================================================
# AGENT_PROVIDER is THE switch: claude | codex | opencode (default "claude",
# the native Claude Agent SDK backend).  Read by .claude/sdk/launch_build.sh
# and handed to build.py as --provider.  Role model maps, Serena transport and
# port, the terminal callback sidecar, and the interactive-subagent model sync
# all key off it, so flipping this ONE line moves the whole pipeline.
#
# 1. COMBOS.  Only these two variables choose a backend + model family:
#
#   Target harness + models          AGENT_PROVIDER  OPENCODE_MODEL_PROVIDER
#   ------------------------------   --------------  -----------------------
#   Claude Code (native SDK)         claude          (ignored)
#   Codex                            codex           (ignored)
#   OpenCode -> AI Commons (Claude)  opencode        (empty)
#   OpenCode -> Go native (DeepSeek) opencode        go
#   OpenCode -> DeepSeek API key     opencode        deepseek
#
#   Resulting opus-tier / sonnet-tier models per combo are defined in the role
#   maps: .claude/sdk/runtime.py (claude), runtime_codex.py, runtime_opencode.py.
#
# 2. WHICH OTHER VARIABLES APPLY.  Each is documented at its own definition
#    below; this is only the index of what matters for which provider.
#
#   Variable                          claude  codex  opencode
#   -------------------------------   ------  -----  --------
#   SDK_CONDA_ENV                     REQ     REQ    REQ
#   SDK_SERENA_PORT      (SSE)        yes     -      -
#   CODEX_SERENA_PORT    (HTTP)       -       yes    -
#   OPENCODE_SERENA_PORT (HTTP)       -       -      yes
#   CODEX_THREAD_ID                   -       callbk -        (ambient in Codex)
#   OPENCODE_SESSION_ID               -       -      REQ      (else silent finish)
#   OPENCODE_SERVE_PORT/USER/PASSWORD -       -      callbk
#   CODEX_MODEL / _REASONING_EFFORT   -       opt    -
#   OPENCODE_MODEL / _VARIANT         -       -      opt
#   *_JSON_STREAM_LIMIT               -       opt    opt
#   CODEX_EVENT_RESUME=0              -       opt-out -
#   OPENCODE_EVENT_RESUME=0           -       -      opt-out
#
#   Only codex and opencode get a terminal callback sidecar.  Under claude you
#   rely on watchdog.sh plus an armed progress Monitor.
#
# 3. INTERACTIVE (non-SDK) SUBAGENTS.
#
#   claude    Agent tool's own `model` param + the crew role map.  Nothing to
#             sync: .claude/agents/ is empty by design.
#   codex     .codex/agents/*.toml `model` field, generated by
#             scripts/sync_codex_agents.py.
#   opencode  .opencode/agents/*.md frontmatter `model:`, generated by
#             scripts/sync_opencode_agents.py.
#
#   launch_build.sh runs the matching sync automatically before each build, so
#   interactive subagents match the models SDK builds use.  NEVER hand-edit
#   those generated files -- change the variable and re-run the sync.
#
# 4. THE FAILURE MODE TO KNOW.  Shell env beats this file, always.  An exported
#    AGENT_PROVIDER or OPENCODE_MODEL_PROVIDER silently outranks what you set
#    here (measured 2026-08-12: a stale exported OPENCODE_MODEL_PROVIDER=go kept
#    selecting DeepSeek after .env said otherwise).  launch_build.sh now prints
#    `provider: <x> (from shell env|.env|default)` on every launch and warns
#    when the two disagree -- read that line to confirm the switch took.
# ==========================================================================
# AGENT_PROVIDER=claude

# Conda environment the pipeline orchestrator AND agents run cogwheel in.
# Must contain both `cogwheel` and a compatible `claude-agent-sdk` for the
# Claude backend (see .serena/memories/pipeline_environment_setup.md). The
# Codex backend uses the installed `codex` CLI and does not add a Python SDK
# dependency. The OpenCode backend uses the installed `opencode` CLI.
# Consumed by .claude/sdk/launch_build.sh and the git hooks. Required — builds
# fail immediately if unset. Copy this file to .env and set it.
# SDK_CONDA_ENV=cogwheel_310

# Optional Codex backend overrides. By default the shared pipeline routes
# scientific-authority roles to gpt-5.6-sol/high and bounded support roles to
# gpt-5.6-terra/medium. A global override replaces every role; a role-specific
# override (for example CODEX_MODEL_TEST_DEV) takes precedence over the global
# value. Role keys are the uppercase names under .codex/agents/.
# CODEX_MODEL=
# CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT=high
# CODEX_MODEL_TEST_DEV=
# CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT_TEST_DEV=
#
# Maximum bytes in one newline-delimited `codex exec --json` event. Whole-file
# tool results can exceed asyncio's 64 KiB default; the adapter defaults to
# 8 MiB. Increase only if a role emits a larger single event.
# CODEX_JSON_STREAM_LIMIT=8388608

# TCP port for the Claude SDK pipeline's shared Serena SSE server (default 8322).
# Set a different port on machines where a sibling repo's pipeline (e.g.
# gw_detection_ias) also runs builds: both hardcoding 8322 makes
# simultaneous builds collide at startup, and each repo's watchdog kills
# whatever listens on its port. Consumed by launch_build.sh, .claude/build
# (exported), .claude/sdk/agents.py (SerenaManager), and watchdog.sh.
# SDK_SERENA_PORT=8323

# TCP port for the Codex pipeline's shared Serena Streamable HTTP server. Keep this
# distinct from SDK_SERENA_PORT so Claude and Codex builds can run
# simultaneously without binding or watchdog collisions.
# CODEX_SERENA_PORT=8324

# TCP port for the OpenCode pipeline's shared Serena Streamable HTTP server. Keep
# this distinct from SDK_SERENA_PORT and CODEX_SERENA_PORT so all three providers
# can run builds simultaneously without binding or watchdog collisions.
# OPENCODE_SERENA_PORT=8325

# Optional OpenCode backend overrides. By default the shared pipeline routes
# scientific-authority roles to claude-v4.6-opus/high and bounded support roles
# to claude-v4.6-sonnet/medium. A global override replaces every role; a
# role-specific override (for example OPENCODE_MODEL_TEST_DEV) takes precedence
# over the global value. Role keys are the uppercase agent names.
# OPENCODE_MODEL=
# OPENCODE_VARIANT=high
# OPENCODE_MODEL_TEST_DEV=
# OPENCODE_VARIANT_TEST_DEV=
#
# Maximum bytes in one newline-delimited `opencode run --format json` event.
# Whole-file tool results can exceed asyncio's 64 KiB default; the adapter
# defaults to 8 MiB. Increase only if a role emits a larger single event.
# OPENCODE_JSON_STREAM_LIMIT=8388608

# Tidier scheduling. By default the Tidier is a POST-COMMIT ADVISORY role and
# its in-DAG build step is SKIPPED (it previously ran last over the whole build
# diff and its error_max_turns finalization could kill the DAG via the anyio
# cancel-scope bug). Set SDK_RUN_TIDIER=1 to opt the in-DAG tidier back in.
# SDK_SKIP_TIDIER=1 remains honored as a hard override that always skips it.
# SDK_RUN_TIDIER=1

# OpenCode model tier -- see the COMBOS table in the header for which value
# selects which family.  ONLY consulted when AGENT_PROVIDER=opencode.
#
# Concrete model strings live in the role maps in runtime_opencode.py
# (AI_COMMONS_/GO_/DEEPSEEK_ROLE_MODELS).  They use the "provider/model" form;
# a bare "deepseek-v4-flash" fails to resolve.  Consumed at import time by
# runtime_opencode.py, which falls back to reading this file when the shell env
# is unset, and exported by launch_build.sh for the build subprocess.
#
# Why the frontmatter is generated rather than model-less: an earlier design
# left .opencode/agents/*.md without a `model:` line so interactive subagents
# inherited the session model.  That was replaced because inheritance cannot
# express per-role tiers (opus-tier Architect vs sonnet-tier Librarian).
# Under AGENT_PROVIDER=claude this is all moot: interactive Claude subagents
# take their model from the Agent tool's own `model` parameter and the crew
# role map, not from any .opencode file.
# OPENCODE_MODEL_PROVIDER=go

# OpenCode serve credentials + callback session for build notifications.
# OPENCODE_SERVE_PORT=4096
# OPENCODE_SERVER_USERNAME=opencode
# OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD=change-me
# OPENCODE_SESSION_ID=ses_...
